From fcd4ffbf8a5d3d19ed83a9199f96b71257a60774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:23:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grate: flush_region of a mapped range is a no-op

grate_resource_transfer_flush_region() was a stub that logged "GRATE
TODO" for every call when GRATE_DEBUG had "unimplemented". The state
tracker calls it for every explicit-flush map, which includes the
upload manager's map of a user vertex array on each draw, so a game
that draws from client arrays printed it once per draw: 254431 lines
in a 43 MB log in a few minutes of Xash3D (Half-Life), which also made
the game very slow while the log was written and buried every other
message.

The mapping is the buffer object itself (a MAP_SHARED mmap, no staging
copy), so there is nothing to write back. Use Mesa's no-op
u_default_transfer_flush_region.

Checked: libgallium builds; xash3d on the tablet with the candidate
library (sha 368405ce5d57) logs 0 flush_region lines (the same run had
254431 before) and the walls, floors and characters render.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_resource.c | 12 +++---------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_resource.c
index c563cdb4560..161fc7c6c93 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_resource.c
@@ -116,14 +116,6 @@ grate_resource_transfer_map(struct pipe_context *pcontext,
    return ret;
 }
 
-static void
-grate_resource_transfer_flush_region(struct pipe_context *pcontext,
-                                     struct pipe_transfer *transfer,
-                                     const struct pipe_box *box)
-{
-   grate_unimplemented();
-}
-
 static void
 grate_resource_transfer_unmap(struct pipe_context *pcontext,
                               struct pipe_transfer *transfer)
@@ -896,7 +888,9 @@ grate_context_resource_init(struct pipe_context *pcontext)
    grate_trace();
    pcontext->buffer_map = grate_resource_transfer_map;
    pcontext->texture_map = grate_resource_transfer_map;
-   pcontext->transfer_flush_region = grate_resource_transfer_flush_region;
+   /* the mapping is the buffer object itself, there is no staging copy
+    * to write back */
+   pcontext->transfer_flush_region = u_default_transfer_flush_region;
    pcontext->buffer_unmap = grate_resource_transfer_unmap;
    pcontext->texture_unmap = grate_resource_transfer_unmap;
    pcontext->buffer_subdata = u_default_buffer_subdata;
-- 
